{"type":"standard","title":"Richard Ojeda","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Richard Ojeda</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q30121703","titles":{"canonical":"Richard_Ojeda","normalized":"Richard Ojeda","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Richard Ojeda</span></span>"},"pageid":54217799,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Richard_Ojeda_shirt.jpg/330px-Richard_Ojeda_shirt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":330},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/eb/Richard_Ojeda_shirt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":3036,"height":3036},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1374212214","tid":"e3a98d4a-ad29-11f1-b198-8569111bfcc1","timestamp":"2026-09-10T15:11:25Z","description":"American politician and military officer (born 1970)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_Ojeda","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_Ojeda?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_Ojeda?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Richard_Ojeda"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_Ojeda","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Richard_Ojeda","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_Ojeda?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Richard_Ojeda"}},"extract":"Richard Neece Ojeda II is an American politician and retired United States Army major who served in the West Virginia Senate representing the 7th district from January 2017 until January 2019. A member of the Democratic Party, he ran a brief campaign for President of the United States in the 2020 election.","extract_html":"<p><b>Richard Neece Ojeda II</b> is an American politician and retired United States Army major who served in the West Virginia Senate representing the 7th district from January 2017 until January 2019. A member of the Democratic Party, he ran a brief campaign for President of the United States in the 2020 election.</p>"}